Subject: [PATCH 03/10] feat: the onboarding becomes the first real attention
 source
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The onboarding has worked since phase 7 — the client answers, the form
saves itself, submitting closes the stage. What was missing was the way in.
The route is not in the navigation, no screen linked to it, and a client
with a draft submission opened the portal with no way to continue. The
pending item existed and reached nobody.

Only draft is the client's turn. not_started means the agency has not
opened it yet and only the agency can, so asking the client to act on it
would be noise wearing the costume of care — a boundary test asserts the
client cannot open their own submission, which is why that state produces
nothing. submitted and unsupported are equally silent.

Reading it needs one column. The existing client read makes four queries
because the screen has to build the form; the home only asks whether it is
the client's turn, and paying for the whole catalogue on every open to show
a numeral is the wrong trade. Same guard, same stage lookup, same state
function — a smaller projection, no new column and no new policy.

Whether the source applies is derived from the journey template rather than
written as a type check against social. Both expressions agree today, but
the second ages the moment a new journey gains the stage, and it would age
silently by no longer asking for an onboarding that exists.

